From: port_ios lavender
Subject: [PATCH 0200] lavender: USB device (DWC3) on SDM660 + live log

sweet_usb.c (0072-0077) was compiled for LAVENDER (it inherits
ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) but with the SM7150 addresses, and nothing called
it: its only caller is sweet_ufs_init(), which never runs on an eMMC board.

- LAVENDER addresses from the phone's DTB: DWC3 core 0x0a800000, QSCRATCH
  0x0a8f8800, QUSB2 v1 PHY 0x0c012000, GCC 0x00100000 (+0x94000); GDSC and
  branch clock offsets from Linux gcc-sdm660.c.
- QUSB2 v1 register readout (PLL lock, power-down) instead of the v2 one.
- sweetusb=3 (lavender, experimental): enable the USB30 GDSC and branch
  clocks from the GCC when ABL left them off (recovery-partition boot).
  No RCG, reset, PMIC regulator or PHY tuning writes.
- Force GCTL.PrtCapDir=device before the device soft reset if needed.
- Live log reads the santoni_sdhci.c console ring (the sweet_ufs.c ring is
  empty on SANTONI/LAVENDER): new santoni_log_copy()/santoni_log_position(),
  placed before santoni_sdhci_rootdev(), away from the ring writer.
- Call sweet_keys_init() and sweet_usb_probe() from IOFindBSDRoot on
  LAVENDER, after the eMMC probe (sweet_usb_probe is now idempotent).

Defaults are safe: sweetusb=1 only reads registers and only when the GCC
says the block is powered and clocked. sweetusb=2 starts the CDC-ECM
gadget (ue0 192.168.7.2/24, UDP log to 192.168.7.1:5140).
diff --git a/bsd/dev/santoni_sdhci.c b/bsd/dev/santoni_sdhci.c
index 2de2143..ab87e5a 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/santoni_sdhci.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/santoni_sdhci.c
@@ -4893,6 +4893,38 @@ santoni_sdhci_probe(void)
 	return init_error;
 }
 
+/*
+ * 0200: readers of the console ring for the USB live log
+ * (bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c, sweetusb=2). Copy bytes [*pos, total), at most
+ * max; a reader that fell more than the ring behind skips ahead. Never
+ * blocks and never prints. Kept away from the ring writer, which later
+ * patches rework.
+ */
+uint32_t santoni_log_copy(uint64_t *pos, char *out, uint32_t max);
+uint64_t santoni_log_position(void);
+
+uint32_t
+santoni_log_copy(uint64_t *pos, char *out, uint32_t max)
+{
+	uint64_t total = os_atomic_load(&santoni_log_total, relaxed);
+
+	if (total - *pos > SANTONI_LOG_SIZE) {
+		*pos = total - SANTONI_LOG_SIZE;
+	}
+	uint32_t n = (uint32_t)MIN((uint64_t)max, total - *pos);
+	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+		out[i] = santoni_log_ring[(*pos + i) % SANTONI_LOG_SIZE];
+	}
+	*pos += n;
+	return n;
+}
+
+uint64_t
+santoni_log_position(void)
+{
+	return os_atomic_load(&santoni_log_total, relaxed);
+}
+
 /* Root device for rd=emmcroot0 (IOFindBSDRoot). */
 int santoni_sdhci_rootdev(dev_t *dev);
 
